From 0af63df7cf7eae019d7b45eb74396ae1085584c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 04:55:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01912/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE B1
 (HARNESS-FIRST + REAL-TRAINING ASSERTION) -- FIX + SMOKE the LoRA harness so
 it CANNOT short-circuit. The .391 attempts (exp4222 smoke 14s, exp4223 3-arm
 36.7s) were both DURATION_TOO_SHORT-flagged: the live LoRA training
 short-circuited to a fake-short 'progress' artifact instead of training. FIX:
 a harness smoke whose deliverable is a POSITIVE CONTROL that asserts REAL
 training -- (a) LoRA attaches with >0 trainable params on a NON-Qwen SOTA
 base loaded via standard AutoModelForCausalLM (NOT the custom Gemma4 wrapper
 that produced Gemma4ClippableLinear), (b) >=20 REAL optimizer steps run on a
 fixture, (c) the loss MOVES (final < initial by a margin), (d) wall-clock
 duration > a plausibility floor for >=20 steps on a 12B LoRA. If training
 cannot run for real in-window, emit blocked_* (NOT progress_*) -- the harness
 FAILS LOUDLY. harness_smoke_passed BARE bool. NO full 3-arm here (that is
 B2). NO TRM.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
---
 ops/changelog.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

