+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -9142,3 +9142,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A1 (HEADLINE BUILD; STRENGTHEN) -- BUILD a CROSS-CANDIDATE SET-ENCODER AGGREGATOR for the oracle-distinct ARC verifier, fixing the .391 null's three causes. .391's build (exp4220) was a per-candidate LOGISTIC REGRESSION (scored each candidate in ISOLATION) trained on 14 ACCEPTED / 1782 REJECTED rows (base-rate 0.008, off-fold AUROC 0.779). FIX: (1) CROSS-CANDIDATE features/architecture -- a permutation-invariant set-encoder over the per-task candidate set (Set-Encoder 2404.06912; MSV 2603.03417 cross-sequence; AggLM 2509.06870 review/reconcile) so each candidate is scored CONDITIONED on its competitors (vote basin, cross-candidate agreement, competing transformation families); (2) CALIBRATED imbalance-aware loss (2509.19681: class-weighted/focal + temperature/isotonic calibration + stratified-balanced minibatches) so the 14-positive slice does not wash out; (3) GROW the labeled pool toward >=30 held-out wrong-majority tasks (reuse scripts/exp_verifier_detector_auroc.py:load_arc_rows over the GAP-4 pools; add games if available). Out-of-fold; verifier_is_oracle=false. Report off-fold AUROC + aggregator_trained + learned_verifier_path + wrong_majority_n + held_out_task_n. Honest no-learnable-signal is COMPLETE and still persists for A2. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete_oracle_distinct_arc_aggregator_no_learnable_gain_auroc0.7866; results/experiment_4231_oracle_distinct_arc_aggregator_build.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A2 (THE HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A1 aggregator_trained) -- does the STRONGER cross-candidate AGGREGATOR BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE at power? On a HELD-OUT ARC split (disjoint from A1 folds, target N>=30), rerank with the A1 aggregator (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute demos) vs majority-vote vs a MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the positive-control ceiling) vs a MARGIN-TRIGGERED override (2606.04323 / ARBITER 2605.26172: override vote ONLY when the aggregator margin clears a pre-registered threshold tuned on the A1 fold). The LOAD-BEARING gate: aggregator@1 - vote@1, bootstrap CI95 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists. YES -> the first oracle-distinct verifier win (closes GAP-3-ties-vote; informs the DiffusionGemma gate). TIES-at-power -> a STRONGER null than .391's n=14. No-headroom -> uninformative (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: oracle_distinct_aggregator_ties_vote_with_headroom_at_power; results/experiment_4232_oracle_distinct_arc_aggregator_beats_vote.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A3 (HEADLINE DISAMBIGUATION; independent) -- the SAME oracle-distinct beats-vote test on CODE, where data is BALANCED and power is HIGH. Train a LEARNED pass/fail predictor over sampled code candidates from CACHED corpora (HumanEval/MBPP/EvalPlus rerank pools) using ONLY oracle-distinct features (the candidate code text + cross-candidate agreement -- NO test execution at inference; the hidden-test label is the TRAINING TARGET only, so verifier_is_oracle=false). Then the beats-vote gate: predictor@1 vs vote@1 vs matched control vs oracle@K, task-level bootstrap CI95-excl-0, N as large as the cached pool allows (code has ~0.6 pass-rate vs ARC's 0.008 base-rate -> far less imbalance + far more positives). PURPOSE: disambiguate whether the .391 ARC null was DATA-SPARSITY (code wins) or a real selection-thesis bound (code also ties). Honest null is COMPLETE. STOP re-running CIRCULAR code-execution selection -- this is the oracle-DISTINCT (no-execution) learned predictor. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: code_oracle_distinct_beats_vote; results/experiment_4233_oracle_distinct_code_beats_vote.json
+- 2026-06-15: PHASE B1 (HARNESS-FIRST + REAL-TRAINING ASSERTION) -- FIX + SMOKE the LoRA harness so it CANNOT short-circuit. The .391 attempts (exp4222 smoke 14s, exp4223 3-arm 36.7s) were both DURATION_TOO_SHORT-flagged: the live LoRA training short-circuited to a fake-short 'progress' artifact instead of training. FIX: a harness smoke whose deliverable is a POSITIVE CONTROL that asserts REAL training -- (a) LoRA attaches with >0 trainable params on a NON-Qwen SOTA base loaded via standard AutoModelForCausalLM (NOT the custom Gemma4 wrapper that produced Gemma4ClippableLinear), (b) >=20 REAL optimizer steps run on a fixture, (c) the loss MOVES (final < initial by a margin), (d) wall-clock duration > a plausibility floor for >=20 steps on a 12B LoRA. If training cannot run for real in-window, emit blocked_* (NOT progress_*) -- the harness FAILS LOUDLY. harness_smoke_passed BARE bool. NO full 3-arm here (that is B2). NO TRM. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_lora_training_cannot_run_in_window; results/experiment_4234_verifier_reward_lora_harness_real_training_smoke.json
